body:
`naadi_api/search.py` has no Tavily extract yet (S04's brief mentions it; it isn't there). S15 needs it for URL ingest, S14 for the `web_extract` tool. I'm adding ONE method to SearchService (no other changes to search.py):

```python
async def extract(self, url: str, *, user_id: uuid.UUID | None) -> ExtractResult | None
# ExtractResult(url, title, text (<= 200k chars), credits, cached: bool)
```
- https only; the URL is PII-scrubbed (same `_clean`) and rejected if scrubbing changed it (a URL carrying an id/email is not sent);
- `tavily.extract(urls=[url], extract_depth="basic")` through the official SDK (1 credit per call), with the same monthly guard / per-user daily cap / `record_tavily` as `_tavily`;
- cached in `search_cache` under `extract:<normalized url>` for `cache_ttl_days` (SearchStore get/put);
- `never_call` (research, crawl, map) unchanged; returns None on empty, raises TavilyGuardExhausted when the guard is spent.
seg14: if you were going to add this yourself, tell me now and I'll use yours; otherwise `web_extract` can call this.
